## What changed

**`frontend/src/core/Document.js`**
- `getDocumentsByProjectId(projectId, { withRelations = false })` no longer sends `populate=*`. By default it populates nothing — the Student/Tutor/Coordinator dashboards only read `title/status/version/createdAt`, and `DocumentViewer`'s sibling-version selector only reads `id/version`. With `withRelations: true` (only `ProyectoDetalle`) it adds exactly: `documentFile[fields]=url` (compare popup + timeline), `restoredFrom[fields]=version` (timeline), `comments[fields]=correction,quote` (project PDF).
- `copyDocumentAsNewVersion` (no current consumers) asks only for `fields[0]=id` on `project/documentFile/comments/notifications`, which is all it uses to relink them.
- `getDocumentById` keeps `populate=*` — it's the findOne feeding the viewer, as the story requires.

**`frontend/src/core/Projects.js`** — `getProjectById` asks for `tutor`/`students` with `fields=username,email` only; `populate=*` was dragging every document of the project along.

**`ProyectoDetalle.jsx`** passes `{ withRelations: true }`; `GeneratePdfButton.jsx` comment updated. `Comments.getCommentsByDocument` was already explicit.

**New test** `frontend/src/core/__tests__/populate.test.js` pins the exact `params` both functions send.

## Verification
- `npm run typecheck`, `npx eslint 'src/**/*.{js,jsx}'`, `CI=true npx react-scripts test --watchAll=false` → 14 suites, 77 tests pass.
